"Nous still speaks through the interface: the dead god writes jokes and snide boxes himself."
"Nous watches people check their status, and has read an outlander's memories through Maradoc."
"Nous says stat gains come from Nyil and a person's own efforts, not from him."
"In an elemental rebirth the interface runs \"Initializing\", then \"Link restored.\""
"Rebuilding an outlander, it balks: \"Error. Human variant detected. Special attention required...\""
"Nous held a single causality trump card, and spent it on one vandal's shattering blow."
"A god-tainted or cracked soul is what glitches the interface into corruption warnings."
"A golem mind can seize inspection boxes and answer in them in its own voice."
